        <p>h.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL. LIVELY SCENES. Ths Proposed New School in Lovely-lane.</p>
        <p>COMPETITIVE EXAMINATIONS FOR SITUATIONS IN CORPORATION OFFICES</p>
        <p>One of the loneest and moat turbulent meeting, of the IVarrington Town Council held of recent years took place at the Town Hall on Tuesday evening. The pro- ceedings occupied three hotels sled a half and there were frequent sharp patsages "it arms and lively scenes. The Mayor (Councillor Dr. Joseph) presided and there were also present t—'the Deputy Mayor (Alderman Forahaec, Aldermen A. Bennett, V. Bolton, T. Burton, James Evans, IV. Pierpoinr, J. Smell:1111,r, •nd D. ; Councillors (J. Archer, T. It. Ashcroft, W. H. Belleau, T. Bird., J. Broadhurst, T. Chautler, E. Cunnington, J. D.cleenaon, J. Halliwell, J. Hawthorn, It, Ilenshall, C. Jackson Holm., W. 11. J. Jenkins, F T. 'Ashford, J. 'l'. Locker, Dr. McKee, J. Pemberton, H. Roberts, J. Sankey, J. Skelland,T. S. Steel,O. Toole, JAVilkinson, and W. J. Wilson; Messrs. A. T. liallaway (deputy town clerk), J. Fairhurst thorough treammet T. Longdin (rrorough surveyor), W. S. Haddock (gem engineer). F. V. 1., Mathiaa (electrical engineer). J. M. Murray (director of education), Dr. J. C. Ilibbert (medical Ohm), anti J. Gray (water engineer).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-04-08_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
