        <p>Councillor ROBERTS made no important lugged ion with reference to junior appointments on the Corpora- ion. fie said that the time had come when there melt to be an interchange of opinion I etween the 'ends of the serious committees as to the scale of illaries to be pot in operation in regard to Corporation ;leeks. The adiniesion of boys Into the Corporation wrvice should oho be made a subjt of open con, vetition. lee boye in the elemen• ry schools should lave an opportunity of trying to enter into the service .1 the Corporation, and some scheme might he devirel .y manna of which there should be to many pie a ,pen eve:y yew. Then the head, of demo ants cccli In relieved tram the persiatent .manure which parents h.ought to in Ir upon tern in connection with their boys and here would he no chant, of favouritism, tithough Ee di 1 not thick there had been any. b,war •Boys would then come, in ,on merit</p>
