        <head>Special Correspondence.</head>
        <p>Special Correspondence.</p>
        <p>Trevaughan Village, Carmarthen, April 3rd, 1911. Sirs,—l duly received the trial pot of " Solaro " which you sent me, and thank you rely much. I should have written sooner, but wan waiting until my husband bad applied your preparation for the third time. 1 8111 more thankfal than lean exprese, to be able to say he is a great deal better, in fact he is like a new nian. Ile has been in absolute misery 1, the past two years, always dreading the night coming, as his intense agony prevented him from sleeping. I have spent p ut,d, on all other ointments and lotions, which are largely advertised, and not one of them did him any good. I shall be delighted to recommend " Solar-a" to everymws. As moon as the trial bcz is emptied I shall hare another--Yours gratefully, (Mrs.) E. LEA.AI. To Remedies Limited.</p>
        <p>That which "Solar., " ha, done fr 11r. Leach, it will also do for you. And when you consider it coats von only 71d. to convince you of its wonderful !leafing powers, surely you will give it a trial. " Solavo immediately relieves and permanently cures Eczema (Wet or Dry), Chilblains, Ringworm, Psoriatis, Btickheadn, Pimple., Facial Eruption, Pik'', Has, Ranh, Chafings, Scabies, Burns, and any form of Skin Disease. To prove that " Solaro" will ponitively cure the al,tive without injuiing the tissue, of the akin, we have decided to send to the first 100,000 applicants one Is. 71d. pot of "Solaro" on rect4pt of 7ld. to cover cost of Postage, Packing, Government Stamp. etc. No charge is made kr the compound. , Thin in nuts sample but a Is. 7d. pot Write at once mentioning The Warrington Examiner, and enclose 7ld. to 11E11E1,1Es LIMITLI, 5, Duke Street, Adelphi, London, W.C. You will always be grateful to us.</p>
