      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-04-08_WidnesExaminer_art0055" n="art0055">
        <head>£2OO Grant to Padgate Church.</head>
        <p>£2OO Grant to Padgate Church.</p>
        <p>At their Nat meeting the Ecclealastical Commit sloe- era merle a otnther of grants to augment some of the poor livings M the Liverpool dioorru and to meet honer., ions of a like amount. A sum of £240 was allocated to Christ Church, Padget, The total wawa amounted to over £9,000, this very large amount being mainly due to the anonymous gift of £5,000 to augment floe of the poorest and roost populolttLiverp tol li•ings end ton most generous gift of a house, value at £l,OOO, oCft permonage to St. Nathsosel, Platt Bridge, by Mr. E. C. Ecltlealey.</p>
