      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-04-08_WidnesExaminer_art0056" n="art0056">
        <head>Christ numb, Latchford.</head>
        <p>Christ numb, Latchford.</p>
        <p>Thin is an age which delights In commemorations— ! jubilee., centenarien, bi-centenariee, ter-centenaries 1 Only lent month we were commemoratine the ter- -1 centenary of the inte of the Authorized Version of the Hcle Bible. Chriat Church, Latchford, is thin year (says "Chriet Church Magazine ") to be ridded to the list of institution, commemorating historical eventa The churct was consecrated to July 1111 h, 1061. by Dr. Graham, Bishop of Chester. We shell, therefore, be celebrating during the coming slimmer the 50th Anni- versary of the Consecratlon—tbe Jubilee of theCharch. Some steps must, of course, be taken to celebrate ade- quately no interesting en event. A preliminary meeting of church officers is to I. held ehortly to consider the hest means of comtoemorsting the oictsaion. We Lave all-tatty invited the Bishop of Iho diocese to preach on Sunday, July 16th, and are hoping that he may be able to accept the invitation. We propose to publish In the magaxine doting the nett fee months any ascertainable facts connected with the building, comecration and early history of the church. For these we shall have to rely on extant historical records and tradition, and shall be grateful to any of our readers who can supply on with information on the nobject. We are not even aware who built the church. Too founden modeatla emit all alluaion to themnelves. All they wont in the Inscription on the brans in the chancel is " To the glory of Ood and in affectionate memory of the late Thomas Greenall, of Wilderapool and Ornppenhail, this church watt @motel Anon Domini, 1461:' Mr. Beamont, however, in his " History of I.tchford," tells on that " the (Mr. (treenail 's) family by • joint contribution in the sear 1461 erected upon a site adjoining the school a small but handnon.e atone church, with an ornamental spire, after a good derign." —We stool-1 be glut to know wh the members of thin family were are! whether any of them urn atilt alive to-day.</p>
      </div>
