        <p>For many years now the member. of the Homy- road %Verde art Church have resorted lon one of work in order to give them a credit Saltine° at the end of the financial year and this recurring event again took place on Wednesdey end Thursday. During the year a besting apparatus, far superior to the old one, has been instaLed •t a cost of .C 1 In and conesquently the church ime been under a heavy espente.The isle proved, an was anticipated, a complete success. The Lecture Ilatl ran ertistically arrengsd, the several stalln attractively display hag good/. of noaefol and orna• mental character. The stalls Isere t—Sesting Meeting (plain and fancy 'L'r, Refreshment, Sinner, Guild, Junior Guild and Sunday School. '</p>
        <p>'I here was a good attendance at the opening ceremony on Wednevday afternoon, over which Ceuta la Savage presided. Amongst those present were the Revs. E. H. Keeling and W. Seed, Mr. and (Ire. J. W. Flaysterd (the latter declared the sale open), Alderman 'Donlon, He. Ferguson, Mums. John Upson, I. Johnson, R. Corbett, and F. A. Hook. The Cu ORMAN said he felt, as in old sailor would say, out of Lie soundings—laughter)— but, after all, when he was at Mew/ley-road he was in the right Waco. lie was glad that Mrs. Hayward sa•s to open the sale, for they had known each other n any ynarr. They had crossed the Alp. together and they had a good time, though in all fair.. he [suit say that it was well that Napoleon had crossed them before, for Le led made • good road. (Laughter and applaute . Mrs. II cooAXI, hoptd that the sale crowd be very successful. She thought they ba.l a good church at Ilewsey-road. Of coursejt took • grist deal of money to keep it in. nice condition, but when they thoug`it of he splendid work that was being dose by the church and the school it most make them feel gl Athat they were connected with such plum. (Hear, bear). She had much pleavure in declaring the sale open. lApplause.l Miss Sybil Tinnion then presented Mos. Hay ward with a handsome bouquet and Miss Ena Omar' ▪ button-hole " to Captain Savage Or. FERGUS., proposed • vote of thanks to the chair- man end Mrs. Hayward. With regard to the former he said that be wu always willing to lend moist.ce to the church and Mrs. Hayward sus another excellent worker for Bursoy-road. In ascending Alderman TINNION said that the church, whatever else it mieht be was, • very homely chu oh, and one that was doing en exceedingly good work. It was is wonder to him bow the church kept so healthy, for they had lost by removals uvetal influential mom-</p>
        <p>hero but they still went on creditably. Ife was Rho Nee that the principal people there that afternoon Bewsey road people sod he thought that the comb ticu was • very happy one. The work which was lg. on in • poor diatrict sod eapeci•lly tbe work of Sunday school 'seeded the cordial sopport of U who cetild lefwl tnrir aid.</p>
        <p>The Rev. E. IL Kr•tiati supported the resolte which was heartily carried. THURSDAY'S OPENING CEREMONY. Thursday's opening ceremony was entrusted toe ir mail be,a nod girls, who had teen trained by! Keeling, Miss Winoie Upson and Mr. Osborne Siocl I tibia Emily Cede made a c•pital preeident eel manner In which she took charge or the proceedi made one disposed to think that euch duties had relegated to her before. Miss Bessie Jones demi the sale open and she, too, indulged in a speech el was weitchown. As usual, the children brought I them poises ebbit contained atones they bad pruc front relati,e. and friends end.. the children mart off the dais they placed them upon a tray held Icy Keeling, who was also the recipient of a • though daintily arranged Imoquet presented by ! Dorothy Lingard. Several musical item• which pleasure to the large number in Ike Hall, were twitted. They included : Action song, by five boy• live girl., entitled " the boy and the gin " ; due., ' say" 1.7 Mime. Alice Nurse end May Jones ; ac song,. When I waa a girl you know," by "bout said."; end action song a Mr. Gollywog good-nig Mho Sadler tatting the solo part. Iliac Winnie accompanied throughout the proceeding, in an MSc style. On the proposition of Dr. Fergilson, • he vote of thanks was accorded to the children. The proceeds of the sale amounted to over Lilo.</p>
