        <p>Ebenezer Church. A fair comber of people enjoyed a milendid cot on Monday evening in the Ebenezer Church, li, market-street. Mr. IL Thornton, J.P presided no items submitted included —Recitation by Min Wi Wardle ; action acing by sin girl. ; pianoforte soli Alin Nellie Wardle ; recitation by Alin l)orinllil arrest solo I.y Min Irene Wenn@ ; •iolin solo by Richardson ; action song, entitled " Granny," by • juvenile. ; recitation by Min Lily Hit bert ; piano ' solo by Min II liighy ; dialogue, entitled "Tempel Knights," by sin bum and recitation by Mies 13 Mika A.Willcock noted as accompnin. Wycliffe PS A. TIIE PENCE QUESTION. There was a good meeting on Sunday presided by Mr. Henry Oshorne, who opoke upon " All nen.," Mr IV Cater gave the adheres his so hving " Right thinking of God." To think right. said we roust look to God for Ili, spirit. not 11 own way but jos, as God would have on. Me.,! ouraelvee by others, would not give us right thin but if we bad willing rind obedient minds, thet results will be right roil men would know us b fruits, end efforts. 'lb roe new niembera noel hearty welcome. Nfr Attwell sang •• Great Paradise " end" Into Thy Hands." Mr. Stansfleld " Never lose sight of Job." and "Trust •orl II Mr. Carter real the lissom •nd the Secretny le prayer. The following resolution submitted P.S.A. brother his, ds en Suuday was no and copies ordered to he vent to the Hon. Sir Edward Grey, Posident Taft, Mr II Smith, M.P., and If, W Ward, of the Notion-11Rn hood Council "We the members of Wycliffe I Warrington, hereby express or, goitiflcation pronouncement of Sir Edward Grey in Purport r proposal of President Taft to submit all gnostic difference between the United Kingdom and the U States to Arbitration and urge the Government inf nations to bring the matter to n speedy and sue.</p>
