      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-04-08_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>PICTURES OF THE WEEK.</head>
        <p>PICTURES OF THE WEEK.</p>
        <p>FATAL RAILWAY ACCIDENT. An extraordinary accident occured this week on thz Great Western Railway between Royal Oak and Westboureit Park Stations, resulting in the diath of one passenger and serious injury to another, whilst several were badly skaken. A pssscoger traits travelling at its ordinary speed, while passing a siding, was fouled by a ballast train shunting on to an adjacent line. Our picture chants the hAck at the dantai,e,i by the passenger train.</p>
        <p>CROWN PRINCE OF VICE-ADMIRALDE FAUQUE DENMARK. DE JONQUIERES, The Crown Prince Christian of Den. Who s to represent France at the mark, who is coming to the Coronation Coronation. as the representative of Denmark.</p>
        <p>THE QUEEN VICTORIA MEMORIAL The Queen Victoria Memorial, opposite Buckingham Palace, is now complete and ready for the opening ceremony by the King on May 16th. Our photograph shows the magnificent figure of Victory," cad in gilded bronze, with the attendant figures of Constancy"° and .Coarage," which crowns the monument, which this week has been disclosed by the removal Of the scaffolding and wooden hoarding. It will be remembered that the base and lower portent were completed and opened to the public in May, 1909.</p>
