        <p>ESTICKS.</p>
        <p>"Ay," it is finished" echoed Bede his great and eager spirit had fled. KING ALFRED. AS. TRANSLATOR</p>
        <p>-- Long years of Danish invasion swei all traces of the work of Bede, and his survived only in the lives of the pee fell to the great King Alfred to be t translator of the Bible, and his gre: breathed the desire "that all the fi youth of his kingdom should emplol selves in nothing till they could re the English Scripture." More than that he placed the law as first among the laws of Englan fine old document begins: ALFRF.D'S DOOMS . . .</p>
        <p>The dooms which the Almighty spake to Moses, and gave him to ki after our Saviour Christ came to ei said He came not to break or forbid keep them. The Lord was speaking these NV Moses and then said, lam the Lord thy God—l led the the land of Egypt and its thraldom. Love thou not other strange Gods Honour thy father and thy motile the Lord gave thee, that thou be to on earth.</p>
