        <p>fellow scribes England re eyed fe time a complete versior of the True, Wycliffe knew no Greek i It is to be doubted whether an England did. But he had Jerome and this was turned into ti language of the day. Never he never resting,undaunted by the tl Church, he toiled at his self-in until the last word was wri "preaching friars" carried the r the serfs of Leicestershire and light in England which has nevei out.</p>
        <p>NICHOLAS DE HEREFORI How far Wycliffe was hel impossible now to say, but its that he incorporated the work of had set their hand to the same te of them, Nicholas de Hereford, WI knowledge and it is said that Old Testament was translated b illustrating the English of the showing how this old versi the ideas of the original we qua 23rd Psalm as rendered by Nichc The Lord governeth me nod shall lacke : in the place of leen ful mite. Over tratir of fulfillin me; my teml he ronsertide. He upon me the sties of rightwis name. For 'rid and if 1 abal go i of the shadove of deth ; 1 sba evelis, for thou lilt with me. Thi etaf ; the ban comfortid me. n redi in thi ninhte a bord ;ug trublyn me. Thou hut myche fat bed and my chalia makende Is right cler it is. And tbi mercy els me ; elle the dayis of my lit. An in the bons of the Lord in to the le</p>
        <p>EXAMPLES FROM WYCLII From Wyclife'. New Testame some of the Beatitudes. Blessid ben pore men in apirit, fo of hevenes herne. Illessid ben inylde men, for welde the ert he. Bleasid ben thei that mornen, be come forbol. Diesel I ben thei that hoe re right wisnesse for thei echelon be Blessid ben merciful men, for th</p>
        <p>If fetish] ben thei that ben of •• thei echulen se God. As an example of his style we copy Matthew 3 1-6. In thilke dayee came Joon IL] in the desert of Jude, saying, ft for the kyngdom of heavenw Forsoythe this i he of whom it it the prorhete, a .vice of a cryi Make ye redy the wayee of the rightful the patties of hyme. Fc Joon fluid° cloth of the ',eerie of girdil of slut, about hie leendi mete stereo loeutnie and bony Thaws, Jerusalem weals out to h, and al the contra about. Jordan: crymened of hym in Jordan, boo, By its association with Wyc worth has become an Englisl numbers amongst its treasure from which he preached, the table at which he ministered and candlesticks which form furniture during the long slow translation by which he wi remembered. The church is so that we can see it as Wycliffe and study the fresco paintings his eyes must have rested wh to the villagers the words whi travelled across the sea shiree John Huss and Martin Luther Europe into the greatest and I(</p>
