        <p>Bedridden for Months, Exhausted and with Nerves Shattered; New Vitality was put into his Veins by Dr. Williams Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>Quite a public character is a way is Mr. William Jenkins, who has charge of the carrier's conveyance running daily between Warmley and Briatol. Wien some time ago an attack of Influenza seized him he expected ta throw off the disorder readily ; but events proved in his ease se in E 0 many others brought to light that the deadliest danger of Influenza lire in the after-effects so difficult to dispel.</p>
        <p>For several mouths Mr. Jenkins lay prostrated at home, nothing Letter than a wreck of a msn Now, Laving taken up kin Gunnery duties again, he feels that be ought to ray a tribute to Dr. Williams'Pink Pills, to which alone he owe, bin splendid recovery. Describing the circumstances of Lis cme to a repeater recently, Mr. Jenkins stated —"fly: troubles began with a sadden attack of Influenza ; the fever left me with dreadful headaches and rains in all my bones. Soon I fell weather and had to remain in bcd. Whenever I moved shocks of pain Sow all over me, and I soon lucerne no helphss that I had to be lifted about like a child. Later, a dreadful sinking sermst'on came over are. My heart used to thump no wildly that it frightened me. One specialist showed great concern about my heart and weakness ; but treatment seemed to do me no god.</p>
