        <p>INDEPENI.F.NT MITHOOIsTA.—The usual monthly P.S.A. ens held in this Owe on Stuntay afternoon. last, presided Ones by Mr. SoiOtool3 Briggs. A solo entitled " Letting on the everlasting Arm," as. very ably sung by Ml,s Runcorn, and Mist Kenyon was equelly successful in her singing of " Jew, loner of my soul." Mr. E. I tart on sang vary sweetly "the !levee of Rest "and "Ile died of a broken heart," and Miss Rancor, also sang "In tPlId1( companion and wonderful love." A duet entitled Eternity is near" was also excellently rendered by Miss Burton and Mr. E, Barton. Miss Griffiths can the accurot waist.</p>
