        <head>Padgate.</head>
        <p>Padgate.</p>
        <p>Wgsr.r.v Grim:l.—The mold monthly devotionel meeting of the Wesley (,uilzl wee held in the school- room on Monday evening lent, presided over by the Ilee. T. Cladding. A solo entitled " The river of sewer' WWI excellently rendered by Miss Oli•e Cladding. Two Addlelllnti on "Economy tad system in the use of time" by Miss Ilealey anti The selection and use of books " by 'Miss Ji aerie Ward were listened to with much interest and thoroughly appreciated. There wen a good attendance. RPOI COUNCIL—A postponed rneetirg of the Parish Connell to consider the arrangements for the Coronation ,was held in the C.C. echoulroorn on Tueadry evening last. A committee consieting of members of the Parish Ce.ncil end several retepayees with the clerk of the Parish Caincil as secretary was formed to carry out all the necessary arrangements. After much discussion It was decided to follow on similar lines to the arrangements which were or eticceeeful at the Coronath. of liing Edward VII. Voluntary contributions ere to be asked torso that the festivities will not I.chargeelde to the rates. SCNIIA V It:. 0001--A farewell meeting end hot-pot supper was held in the schoolroom on Wednesday evening lest, when a large number of old and present scholars of the Sunday school assembled together for the biet time in the old school. After full justice had been done to the hot.pots which had been kindly given by members of the congregation, Sc., a meeting wee held, presided over by Alder- man Bennett, J.P. Mr. Crlnston who is see of the oldest scholars raid hie recollection went hack to the old chapel before the present one was built and he told some very amusing and interesting stories of the olden days. lierniuisences of the present school were given by Alderman Bennett, Mr. fined., On. Bennett Bull Alr. Wright, which were listened to with eager interest hy all p it and bronght tuck to the old scholers who note eseembled, meaty happy th, tights of days gone by. A solo entitled Two eyee of grey" wen very evreetly song by 'Mrs. 1,. Bennett Intl a quartett entitled "Departure" was very ably rendered by 11Ire. Gledding, Miss 0, Oladding, Rev. T. °bidding and Mr. Newton. The teak of demolishing the old school was then commenced, Alderman Bennett being rooked to knock the first brick out. Several bricks were afterwards knocked out by the old and present scholaes and the meeting broke up alter spending a very enjoyable evening. The new Ildlonl is expected to be complete by September.</p>
