        <p>ST. HELENS.</p>
        <p>ST. IrELENS MEDICAL OFFICER'S NEW POST. Dr. Btichsn, who has been medical officer for St. Helens hitters 1904, has been appointed reediest officer fhr Went lierkshiie. Dr. Buchan nes formerly assistant med;cal officer at Hamilton, I acerkshire. Ilia term of office at St. Helens has been marked by great ability and, conscientious work. He recently I oalifled as a rrr, ister, and his wife is the daughter of Alderman 3. Forster, the Chinese Consul.Gecersl for England. TI a misty of his new post hegins at £950, and his head- trimmers will Ia Rending, last wrek The assistant medical officer of Si. Helens. Dr. J. J. Peterson, was sppointml medical officer ft, Emit Berkshire. St. Helens will thos lose loth of its reediest olficers, who by. coincidence hare been sppointed to r eighbouriog distiicts in the mole county' Dr. Paterson's district will include Windsor, and his headquarters will be Maidenhead. Ile bee been at St. Helens just over two year. 115•511... nr.SI,!. INS Will 111611 ER Skr.%Rv.</p>
        <p>The St. Helens Town Council, in committe:e. on Wedneaday, considered the pr +Rion created by ths appointment of both the medical Ellice, sod deputy medical officer to Ether situations. The Health Com- mittee had met the previous evening and presented to the Council a resolution that, with anew to retaining the services of Dr. Buchan, the Council be recom- mended to increase his salary for the present appointments from SC® per annum to £7IO per annum as from the 15th June, 1911, sod to £750 per annum as from the 15th Jute, Itll3, and not to make .y !ethic- tion in his eatery when the Local Government Beard cease to consent to hiscontitined appointment as public analyst in addition to his appointment of medical officer of health, which the Boar I pet pose to do when the populat ion of the borough reaches 100,000. Alter n discussion, the Council by a majority con- firmed the committee's minutes, and it is understood that the new position is acceptable to Dr. Buchan, and that he will retain the post of medical officer of the be tough. • CORONATION AItRANt.ENIENTS FOR ST.</p>
