        <p>The Coronation Proceeding. Committee of the St. Itch ns Corporation have decided to hold a school children's treat, in which all the public elementiry schools children in the bototigh and those ettending the Moss Bank, Christ Church, Eccleston, and Eccleston- lane Ende School shall take pared° consiat of open-air fetes in the Queen'. Recreation Ground, 'natio Death Park, Sutton Perk, (lathe!' Perk, and Parr Recreation Ground, at which bands, entertaitimenis, and daylight fireworks or ill to peovided. The children le ill walk in procession Boca their schools to the particular path allotted to them,and af or joining in the hinging of the National Anthem to he set at liberty to enjoy tberoseleos in the park in their own any. A grent of (id. per child on the registefs of schools in the borough is to teemed° with. view to providing a meal for the children before the processions. The loon Dell is to be decorated, and priges are to be offered for the best denoroted businves premises, cad pinto house.. An old folks' trent is to Its, aeran4ed. Toe Mayor (Alder- man Beecham, will pea sent a souvenir of tbe Coronation to be children of the elementary schools. ALLEGED ROBBERY FROM MINISTER'S HOUSE. Hugh Beattie, fitter, of 10, Gerard-street, Widnes, was emended at S. Ilelens on Monday n • charge of hooking end entering the residence of the Rev. W. flolroyd, Baptist enibister, of 13, Windle,street, and steeling a laily'a gold watch, gold chain, eeirrings, gold ring, pair of gold-rimmed ape ethcleo, gold brooch, and lady's siker bracelet watch, of the value of £25.-11. Chief Consteble said bee., not in a pesition logo on with the case that day, and naked for a remand for a week.—Bea' tie MRS seen in St. Helens at • quarter to three on Saturday afternoon, nose the Lingholfre Hotel, by Inspector Fairhurst, who promptly notified the detective department. That some afternoon Mr. Ilfoiroyd's family left the house locked up Nra little over an holm and when they returned they found thnt the hack door won open. They did not miss anything, and thought little l• hoot the matter mall! Soniay at who,. the jewellery was wanted. They went to the &amp;fewer where it N. kept, and on finding it missing at once reported the mutter to the police.- Knowing that Beattie lia I tee,, in the loon on the Satile,tar, all °Geer weid to Widnes where he will living, and they treced to lila possession a gold watch. At first Beattie stoutly denied that he Ira! been in St. efeiens, h,t he now adniitied it.—The chief constable added that they hoped to trace the other article, —Detect i VP. I oxpoctor Dunn save evid- ence of the eeriest, tat Boothia offered no objection 0 being ri mended a merit.</p>
        <p>TIIE ALL-BI{I.IISH SHOPPING WEEK IN LONDON.</p>
        <p>Saturday night tare the close of be All-British Shopping Week in London, or. I the opinion of its organisers and of merchants sod manuractorent is (says the Press Association; that from an educational point of •iew it has been an mum di fled success. Mr. Parker, of Messrs. Onrnage, said t—" I think, FO far an bringing p•ople out to see the shops, the week has been • great succem It has Lot made the Ft:lsraeli-or incentive in trade that some people anticipated. Taiga it all the way round, it hes been a very tine advertisement for the manufacturers. A g° at demand ban been created for goods that the majority°, people did not anticipate could ha made ia this country. That ens moat ally noticeable in the drapery sod kindred trade..'</p>
