        <p>MONEY HIDDEN IN STOCKINGS. At the Warrington Petty Sessions held on Wednesday before Mre.rs. S. Rigby Armitage in the chair ~ W. I'. Itylnods and It. C. Parr, Mary Hannah Redhead wee charged with,. the Ist not. at Enrlewolvwfor stealing a gold cross and purtrec.taining LI 7s lathe prnpnrty of Mrs. Brought.. The evidence showed that those named and other women err, together in a public:ll,o.e, when Mrs. Broughton went into the lavatory leaving her !mallet containing the stolen property on the table. When she returned she discovered that Ih• cross sod money was missing,so she searched several in the room excepting Mrs. Redhead who had gone ,to soother lavatory. When she cmon hack she was searched but the property was not found. The landlady then turned the women out into the street, turel two or three of them took the defendant's Foots otT and the monoy was found in her stockinge,—A flee of 20s. and costs was imposed.</p>
