        <head>vitetros EDI'</head>
        <p>vitetros EDI'</p>
        <p>ihe Rector and Rome. -In clesing say polite correspondence with Nigher Whittle, %A Lich was brought al out by Roman arnphle to tent to rite and Roman notices in the papers of iny address to the Warr Mgt. Church S. ciety, 1 trial to fix the attention of my readers on the four points in which! hate a-serted that the Church of Iton.e is Us catla,l C, a I OSltiOa ithiCh I still Maintain. I. Ban. Supremacy.—! have preyed the hone. leanness of this claim by the existence at this day of the Eastern Patriarchates and their COttitiittsl protest from the very End against it. 2. The Filioque—l have shown that the addition of this choose in 5149 ens tie chief cause of the me t Schism in 1054, and the subject of a prded again t it Ly Lope Leo 111., Bishop if Rome ii. 8119. 3. Consecration. - 1 linie affumed that 1,00 years after Chritt Rime substituted in her Cancn of the Mass for the Invocation of the Moly Ghost, Christ's Declaration of the nature of the Elements after Con- secration, making the recital of the words "This is Sly Body," "1 Ids is Sly Blood," the efficient cause of the Sacramental Change contrary to the urine ma practice cf Chridendorn. 4. Transubstantial ion.— I have shown to the satisfaction, I believe, of every impartial and unprejudiced person that neither Holy Scripture nor the Fathers teach Transubstantiation, and II now quote for the study of every thoughtful reader the words of one I f our greatest modern authorities, Bishop Mandell Creighton, "The Church of Rome is weighted with a doctrine that has lost all meaning because it is connected with it FIN siem of philosophy which is no longer held. Sul;stance and accidents I are now echoes of extinct metaph39lol." Ibis is cruehing and withering, hut it is true and just, and in these days when Rome though on suffer- ance here preturres to dispute the Catholicity of the Church of the land, I feel that the scornful rebuke is needed and deserved.—Vours, La, FREDERIC W. NI lI.LIS.</p>
